This guide shows how to run a red-team operation on the Windows agent using Caldera, generating events that Wazuh will detect.

1- Prepare the Windows Agent

Ensure the Windows 10 agent is installed and connected to Caldera (see 02-windows-agent.md).

Confirm the agent appears as Active in the Caldera web interface.

2- Create an Operation in Caldera

Navigate to Operations → New Operation.

Configure the operation:

Name: Test-RedTeam

Adversary: Choose Sandcat or any pre-defined adversary profile.

Targets: Select your Windows agent.

Executor: PowerShell/Windows.

Click Create Operation.

3- Run a Controlled Attack

Click Start Operation.

Monitor the operation in real-time:

Tasks will execute on the agent.

The agent will perform activities such as:

Ping tests

File creation/modification

Command execution

4- Verify Detection in Wazuh

Access the Wazuh dashboard.

Navigate to Alerts.

Look for events triggered by the agent IP or executed commands.

Example alert: "Windows agent executed ping to suspicious IP".

5- Notes

This simulation uses only safe, controlled scripts from Caldera.

Wazuh should generate alerts according to configured rules.

Once confirmed, these alerts demonstrate the end-to-end detection from a simulated attack on Windows to Wazuh monitoring.
